--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Code that is NOT under the MIT licence above

The MIT licence covers only the code written for LucinaOS. Anything taken from another project stays under that project's
licence, and nothing here relicenses it:

- A file with its own licence or SPDX notice is under that licence. That notice decides, not this file.
- Code derived from Asterinas is under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, as Asterinas is.
- third_party/ holds other projects, each under the licence in its own folder or files.
- Code ported from Linux and other GPL projects stays under the GPL with its notices. Today that is files in
  drivers/lucina-adreno, drivers/lucina-venus, drivers/lucina-qrtr, drivers/lucina-qmi, kernel/lucina-cpubw (GPL-2.0-only),
  kernel/lucina-errseq (GPL-2.0-only, from lib/errseq.c of Linux), services/lucina-surface-rules (GPL-2.0-only, buffer rules after the Linux dma-buf/GEM semantics),
  drivers/lucina-apple-aic (GPL-2.0-or-later, from irq-apple-aic.c
  of Asahi Linux), drivers/lucina-apple-uart (GPL-2.0-only, from samsung_tty.c of Linux),
  drivers/lucina-apple-aic-glue (GPL-2.0-only, from irq-apple-aic.c and arm_arch_timer.c of Linux), drivers/lucina-apple-boot
  (GPL-2.0-only, from arm64 smp_spin_table.c and the simple-framebuffer binding of Linux; follows m1n1 behaviour, nothing copied), fortuna/sim and office/engine (AGPL).
  A program built from such a file is itself bound by that licence.
- Crates under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, as the Asterinas code they extend or the code they were written beside:
  drivers/lucina-audio-ledger, drivers/lucina-audio-wake, drivers/lucina-charge, kernel/lucina-cpufreq, kernel/lucina-crash,
  drivers/lucina-gesture, drivers/lucina-i2c-hid, kernel/lucina-idle, kernel/lucina-irqgate, kernel/lucina-kexec, kernel/lucina-ksyms,
  kernel/lucina-ksyms-build, services/lucina-nav, kernel/lucina-power, kernel/lucina-rcu, kernel/lucina-ring, apps/lucina-shell,
  kernel/lucina-sleep, kernel/lucina-spmi, kernel/lucina-standby, crates/lucina-suspend, kernel/lucina-structmap, kernel/lucina-taskcpu and
  drivers/lucina-wifi-wake.
- drivers/lucina-qcom-services is under the BSD 3-Clause licence.
- apps/lucina-app-desk links lucinadesk-core (gvitolocs/lucinadesk-core), which is under the AGPL-3.0-only. The desk app as built is
  bound by the AGPL.
- Fonts and other assets are under the licence files next to them.

Each file or folder's own notice says where it came from and under which licence.
